  "$comment": "Shared by the backend (backend/test/image-frames.test.ts) and the Rust core: both must reproduce every expected rect exactly (decision 0086). place: the largest rectangle of aspect aspectW:aspectH that fits imageW x imageH, centred on focus (fractions of the image) and moved inside the image. Let wide = imageW*aspectH >= imageH*aspectW. If wide: exactW = imageH*aspectW/aspectH, exactH = imageH; else exactW = imageW, exactH = imageW*aspectH/aspectW. All in f64. Rounding: w = round(exactW) and h = round(exactH), each clamped to [1, imageW] and [1, imageH]; round is half up (floor(v+0.5)). x = floor(focus.x*imageW - exactW/2) and y = floor(focus.y*imageH - exactH/2), each clamped to [0, imageW-w] and [0, imageH-h]. Expected values are integer pixels. override: a rect of fractions {x,y,w,h} as pixels: w = round(rect.w*imageW) and h = round(rect.h*imageH), each clamped to [1, image size]; x = floor(rect.x*imageW) and y = floor(rect.y*imageH), each clamped to [0, imageW-w] and [0, imageH-h].",
